  "evidence": [
    {
      "topic": "Document root",
      "finding": "startWemo.sh line 5 launches wemoApp -webdir /tmp/Belkin_settings/. ControlleeDeviceStart preserves argument 4 at 0x1df5c; if null substitutes string 0x50104 (/tmp/Belkin_settings) at 0x1e1a8..0x1e1b4; passes root to UpnpSetWebServerRootDir at 0x1e260..0x1e268."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Normal GET path",
      "finding": "Patched webserver.c decodes escapes then removes dot segments at lines 1094..1095; concatenates document root at 1176..1177; calls realpath at 1198 and checks strstr(abspath,gDocumentRootDir.buf) at 1200. This substring check is not a rigorous containment guarantee; no claim of complete traversal resistance."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Raw flash nodes",
      "finding": "get_file_info at patched lines 543..552 accepts directories or regular files and rejects other types. Character/block flash device nodes are not supported by this normal serving path. This still holds independently of a hypothetical path-containment weakness."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Virtual callbacks",
      "finding": "ControlleeDeviceStart 0x1df6c..0x1dfa0 sets get_info=GetFileInfo, open=OpenWebFile, write=PostFile; read/seek/close zero. Calls UpnpSetVirtualDirCallbacks at 0x1e354..0x1e35c, UpnpAddVirtualDir with ./ at 0x1e408..0x1e410. Bundled upnpapi.c 4198 onward requires each callback and its read setter rejects null. No patch altering those functions was found. This does not establish a working alternate reader. Previously disassembled GetFileInfo/OpenWebFile/PostFile are logging stubs."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Uploads",
      "finding": "040-restrict-posts.patch allows only /tmp/Belkin_settings/rules.db and icon.jpg and imposes a 256KiB entity-length check. These are state-changing uploads, not firmware backup or arbitrary application installation. Not tested live."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Export/symlink search",
      "finding": "Scoped scan of packaged SNSV2 text and SNSV2/base-files archive links found no flash-export file or document-root link to raw flash. Startup writes boot_A_args to /tmp/bootArgs, outside the documented web root. Other low-level MTD read symbols are kernel-driver code, not HTTP export handlers. Not exhaustive proof about generated files or 11565."
    }
  ],
  "conclusion": "No safe firmware/bootloader export mechanism established through these HTTP paths. No exact 11565 image or matching bootloader obtained. No reliable Wi-Fi-only recovery established.",
  "recovery_gap": "Even a successful read of flash would provide backup bytes, not a means to restore those bytes when kernel or Wi-Fi no longer works. Bootloader transport/rollback must be independently established before any replacement firmware.",
  "next_evidence_needed": [
    "Exact 11565 HTTP/application implementation or proven nonmutating acquisition mechanism",
    "Matching bootloader implementation and boot environment",
    "Verified recovery independent of replacement kernel and radio"
  ],
